#: ../../library/sqlite3.rst:2256
msgid ""
"By default, :mod:`!sqlite3` represents each row as a :class:`tuple`. If "
"a :class:`!tuple` does not suit your needs, you can use "
"the :class:`sqlite3.Row` class or a custom :attr:`~Cursor.row_factory`."
msgstr ""
"Voreingestellt stellt :mod:`!sqlite3` jede Zeile als :class:`tuple` dar. "
"Passt ein :class:`!tuple` nicht zu deinen Bedürfnissen, kannst du die "
"Klasse :class:`sqlite3.Row` oder eine eigene :attr:`~Cursor.row_factory` "
"verwenden."

#: ../../library/sqlite3.rst:2261
msgid ""
"While :attr:`!row_factory` exists as an attribute both on "
"the :class:`Cursor` and the :class:`Connection`, it is recommended to "
"set :class:`Connection.row_factory`, so all cursors created from the "
"connection will use the same row factory."
msgstr ""
":attr:`!row_factory` gibt es zwar als Attribut sowohl auf "
